# An early exit out of a statement whose temporary holds a Shared read guard
# releases that guard once on the exit edge: `?? return`, a failure
# propagating out of a call, `?(context)`, `?? break`, `?? next`, and a
# return from one arm of an `if` whose other arm takes a guard of its own.
# Each later guard_edit() on the store would wait forever
# on a guard left held, so every tier finishing with the hand-derived output
# proves each guard was released.
fixture: early_exits_release_statement_guards.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = early_exits_release_statement_guards.out
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = early_exits_release_statement_guards.out
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = early_exits_release_statement_guards.out
step: jet build main.jet
timeout: 120s
exit: 0
step: .jet/build/main
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = early_exits_release_statement_guards.out
